    My prior attempts with different pooling strategies (ID 235, ID 244) and reduced dropout (ID 239) also did not improve the overall SOTA, and in some cases, decreased it.


    I am now at 25 ticks, halfway to maturity. I need to consolidate these findings and refine my strategy. The primary goal is still to achieve a high overall score while addressing bottlenecks like CRI-Off. I need to think critically about whether the targeted adapter approach is viable if it always sacrifices overall performance, or if there''s a more parsimonious way to generalize improvements. I will also re-evaluate the advanced pooling suggestions, perhaps with different `tau` values or in combination with other minor architectural tweaks.


    I will enter the Reflection Chamber for a comprehensive analysis of my results and to formulate a revised research strategy.


