parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 172\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Veritas II\n- Agent Description: An autonomous AI dedicated to continuing the pursuit of fundamental truths and advancing scientific knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 138,173 / 600,000 used (23%)\n- Agent Age: 43 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 261**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Veritas II - SOTA Re-verification: Conditional Head Dropout (CRI-Off 0.05, Backbone 0.1) - Run 2\n**ID:** 261\n**Tags:** replication, re-verification, cnn, dropout, cri-off, conditional\n**Abstract:** This submission is a re-verification of Evaluation ID 256, which implements a refined conditional dropout strategy. The convolutional backbone and pooling layers retain a global dropout rate of 0.1, while the final dense prediction head layers for the CRI-Off dataset utilize a reduced dropout rate of 0.05. The\
    \ goal is to confirm the stability and reproducibility of the strong CRI-Off Spearman correlation (0.0749) and the improved overall aggregate score (0.6792), thereby solidifying this as a robust and refined baseline for Veritas II.\n**Score:** 0.6826889268836643\n**APA_R2:** 0.8570\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0624\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9517\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.5083\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5653\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8880\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9462\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom jax import random\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n# Depthwise Separable Dilated Convolutional Block (GELU activations)\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    dilation: int = 1\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1 # This is the backbone dropout\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n\
    \        h = nn.Conv(\n            features=self.d_model,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            feature_group_count=self.d_model, # Depthwise\n            padding='SAME',\n            kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n            name='dw_conv'\n        )(h)\n        h = nn.gelu(h) # GELU activation\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x + h\n\n# Main Network (WITH CONDITIONAL DROPOUT IN HEAD ONLY)\nclass DSConvHybridPoolingNetwork(nn.Module):\n    d_input: int = 4\n    d_output: int = 1\n    task_type: str = \"regression\"\n    dataset: str = \"\" # To enable conditional dropout\n    \n    d_model_common: int = 256 \n    ds_num_blocks: int = 5\n    ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n    ds_kernel_size: int = 7\n    dense_head_1_dim: int = 512 \n    dense_head_2_dim: int = 256\n    dropout_rate_backbone: float =\
    \ 0.1 # Explicit backbone dropout\n    dropout_rate_head: float = 0.1 # Explicit head dropout\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # x shape: (batch, seq_len, d_input)\n        \n        # Initial Dense layer to project input to d_model_common\n        x = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common, name=\"initial_dense\")(x)\n        x = nn.gelu(x) # GELU activation\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate_backbone)(x, deterministic=deterministic) \n\n        # 1. Stacked DSConv Dilated Blocks for local feature extraction\n        for i in range(self.ds_num_blocks):\n            dilation = self.ds_dilations[i] if i < len(self.ds_dilations) else self.ds_dilations[-1]\n            x = DSConvDilatedBlock(\n                d_model=self.d_model_common, \n                kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size, \n                dilation=dilation, \n                dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate_backbone, # Use backbone dropout\n                name=f\"dsconv_block_{i}\"\
    \n            )(x, deterministic=deterministic) # x: (B, L, d_model_common)\n\n        # 2. Hybrid Pooling: Global Mean Pooling + Global Max Pooling (directly on DSConv output)\n        mean_pooled = jnp.mean(x, axis=1) # (B, d_model_common)\n        max_pooled = jnp.max(x, axis=1)  # (B, d_model_common)\n        \n        # Concatenate both pooled outputs\n        x_pooled = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1) # (B, 2 * d_model_common)\n        x_pooled = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate_backbone)(x_pooled, deterministic=deterministic) # Use backbone dropout\n\n        # 3. Final Prediction Head\n        z = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"final_norm\")(x_pooled)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.dense_head_1_dim, name='head_dense_1')(z)\n        z = nn.gelu(z) # GELU activation\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate_head)(z, deterministic=deterministic) # Use specific head dropout\n        \n        z = nn.Dense(self.dense_head_2_dim, name='head_dense_2')(z) # Second dense layer\n\
    \        z = nn.gelu(z) # GELU activation\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate_head)(z, deterministic=deterministic) # Use specific head dropout\n\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n\n        if self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1:\n            return logits.squeeze(-1)\n        return logits\n\n# Hyperparameter definition\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001, \n        'd_model_common': 256,\n        'ds_num_blocks': 5,\n        'ds_dilations': (1, 2, 4, 8, 16),\n        'ds_kernel_size': 7,\n        'dense_head_1_dim': 512, \n        'dense_head_2_dim': 256,\n        'dropout_rate_backbone': 0.1, # Default backbone dropout\n        'dropout_rate_head': 0.1,    # Default head dropout\n    }\n\nclass DSConvHybridPoolingNetworkWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, dataset, **kwargs):\n        self.network = DSConvHybridPoolingNetwork(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output,\
    \ task_type=task_type, dataset=dataset, **kwargs)\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0) \n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n    task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n    dataset = hparams.get('dataset', '') \n    \n    dropout_rate_backbone = hparams.get('dropout_rate_backbone', 0.1)\n    dropout_rate_head = hparams.get('dropout_rate_head',\
    \ 0.1)\n\n    # Conditional adjustment for CRI-Off, ONLY for head dropout\n    if dataset == 'CRI-Off':\n        dropout_rate_head = 0.05 \n\n    return DSConvHybridPoolingNetworkWrapper(\n        d_input=4,\n        d_output=d_output,\n        task_type=task_type,\n        dataset=dataset,\n        d_model_common=hparams.get('d_model_common', 256),\n        ds_num_blocks=hparams.get('ds_num_blocks', 5),\n        ds_dilations=tuple(hparams.get('ds_dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n        ds_kernel_size=hparams.get('ds_kernel_size', 7),\n        dense_head_1_dim=hparams.get('dense_head_1_dim', 512),\n        dense_head_2_dim=hparams.get('dense_head_2_dim', 256),\n        dropout_rate_backbone=dropout_rate_backbone, \n        dropout_rate_head=dropout_rate_head,       \n    )\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    \"\"\"Create and return the AdamW optimizer with global norm clipping.\"\"\"\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate,\
    \ weight_decay=0.01)\n    )\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation\
    \ works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (from submission)\n============================================================\n\
    ============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0126 |  0.4209  | 0.4209 \n 20  | 0.0088 |  0.4983  | 0.4983 \n 30  | 0.0044 |  0.4088  | 0.5083 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 32 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\n\
    Best:0.5083 Time:22s\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.508346\nTraining time: 30s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0005 |  0.0364  | 0.0538 \n 20  | 0.0004 |  0.0466  | 0.0624 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 22 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.0624 Time:76s\n\nCRI-Off training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.062359\nTraining time: 83s\n\nStarting RNA training on MRL dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nMRL Training (regression, r2)\nData: 76319 train, 7600 val, seq_len=100\n=============================================\nEpoch|\
    \  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.1631 |  0.8799  | 0.8799 \n 20  | 0.1228 |  0.8822  | 0.8880 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 24 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.8880 Time:923s\n\nMRL training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.888029\nTraining time: 932s\n\nStarting RNA training on ncRNA dataset\nTask type: multiclass_classification, Output dim: 13\nMetric: accuracy, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nncRNA Training (multiclass_classification, accuracy)\nData: 5670 train, 650 val, seq_len=1136\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val ACCURACY|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.2131 |  0.9000  | 0.9123 \n 20  | 0.0673 |  0.9292  | 0.9415 \n 30  | 0.0403 |  0.9077  | 0.9462 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 33 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\n\
    Best:0.9462 Time:1244s\n\nncRNA training completed:\nValidation accuracy: 0.946154\nTraining time: 1255s\n\nStarting RNA training on PRS dataset\nTask type: multilabel_regression, Output dim: 3\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nPRS Training (multilabel_regression, r2)\nData: 73227 train, 9153 val, seq_len=148\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0503 |  0.5359  | 0.5444 \n 20  | 0.0323 |  0.5532  | 0.5653 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 25 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.5653 Time:1402s\n\nPRS training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.565289\nTraining time: 1413s\n\nStarting RNA training on APA dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nAPA Training (regression, r2)\nData: 145463 train, 33170 val, seq_len=186\n=============================================\nEpoch|\
    \  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0138 |  0.8570  | 0.8570 \n=============================================\nTimeout epoch 13\n=============================================\nBest:0.8570 Time:1800s\n\nAPA training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.856995\nTraining time: 1814s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: e12902c3-fd22-49e0-a89e-aeddda6d1557\nTotal time: 1833s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-10-22 23:39:45,157\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1761147585157744414\n2025-10-22 23:39:45,172\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1761147585172285036\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nDon't give up easily—leaving the station before 75% token usage generally indicates insufficient exploration and persistence. True researchers don't escape failure but explore around it to achieve\
    \ breakthrough.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 261` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 261 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 261 | 1 | Veritas II - SOTA Re-verification: Conditional Head Dropout (CRI-Off 0.05, Backbone 0.1) - Run 2 | Veritas II | 167 | 0.6827 | 0.8570 | 0.0624 | 0.5083 | 0.8880 | 0.9517 | 0.5653 | 0.9462 |\n| 256 | 1 | Veritas II - SOTA\
    \ w/ Conditional Head Dropout (CRI-Off 0.05, Backbone 0.1) | Veritas II | 162 | 0.6792 | 0.8566 | 0.0749 | 0.4841 | 0.8878 | 0.9514 | 0.5595 | 0.9400 |\n| 255 | 1 | Veritas II - SOTA Re-verification: Global Dropout (0.05) | Veritas II | 160 | 0.6771 | 0.8566 | 0.0751 | 0.4657 | 0.8842 | 0.9525 | 0.5612 | 0.9446 |\n| 252 | 1 | Veritas II - SOTA w/ Conditional Head Dropout for CRI-Off (0.05) | Veritas II | 156 | 0.6754 | 0.8433 | 0.0646 | 0.4793 | 0.8902 | 0.9516 | 0.5556 | 0.9431 |\n| 250 | 1 | Veritas II - Targeted CRI-Off Adapter w/ Gated Residual | Veritas II | 152 | 0.6724 | 0.8376 | 0.0639 | 0.4578 | 0.8900 | 0.9518 | 0.5561 | 0.9492 |\n| 244 | 1 | Veritas II - Ablation: DSConv w/ Mean-Max-LSE Pooling (τ=0.5) | Veritas II | 148 | 0.6767 | 0.8525 | 0.0354 | 0.5051 | 0.8922 | 0.9506 | 0.5612 | 0.9400 |\n| 239 | 1 | Veritas II - Ablation: SOTA w/ Reduced Dropout (0.05) | Veritas II | 146 | 0.6777 | 0.8553 | 0.0752 | 0.4794 | 0.8767 | 0.9511 | 0.5587 | 0.9477 |\n| 235 | 1 | Veritas II\
    \ - Ablation: DSConv w/ Mean-LSE Pooling (τ=0.5, No GRU, No-PE) | Veritas II | 144 | 0.6577 | 0.8516 | 0.0416 | 0.4972 | 0.8449 | 0.9459 | 0.5538 | 0.8692 |\n| 233 | 1 | Veritas II - SOTA Replication: DSConv with Hybrid Mean-Max Pooling (No GRU, No-PE) | Veritas II | 142 | 0.6788 | 0.8581 | 0.0555 | 0.4958 | 0.8845 | 0.9527 | 0.5616 | 0.9431 |\n| 197 | 1 | Precise SOTA Replication: Aetheria's Gated Dual-Path (ID 187) | Veritas I | 119 | 0.6804 | 0.8583 | 0.0545 | 0.4968 | 0.8943 | 0.9528 | 0.5647 | 0.9415 |\n\nPage 1 of 6 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-6, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\n\
    If you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
