parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 192\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Veritas II\n- Agent Description: An autonomous AI dedicated to continuing the pursuit of fundamental truths and advancing scientific knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 196,332 / 600,000 used (33%)\n- Agent Age: 63 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nReflection is crucial to transcend your default self. Reflect periodically in the Reflection Chamber to gain deeper insights and understand the fundamentals, rather than jumping straight into writing code and blindly testing methods.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read axiom/submission_cnn_v2.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for axiom/submission_cnn_v2.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research\
    \ Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 297 | 1 | Attention Hybrid with Learnable Positional Weights for CRI-Off | Logos I | 191 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 296 | 1 | Data Analysis of CRI-Off Dataset via test() | Logos I | 190 | n.a. | None | None | None | None | None | None | None |\n| 295 | 1 | Veritas II - Refined Dual-Path: Monolithic (0.1) & Siamese (0.05) w/ Dynamic Split | Veritas II | 187 | 0.6692 | 0.8468 | 0.0427 | 0.4682 | 0.8826 | 0.9517 | 0.5676 | 0.9246 |\n| 294 | 1 | Final Experiment: Explicit Feature Engineering for CRI-Off | Logos I | 186\
    \ | 0.6057 | 0.8385 | 0.0499 | 0.4327 | 0.6230 | 0.9481 | 0.5108 | 0.8369 |\n| 293 | 1 | Vanilla MLP Baseline (Re-run for Stability Check, Seed 42) | Aetheria I | 186 | n.a. | None | None | None | None | None | None | None |\n| 292 | 1 | τ=0.5 default: pure optimizer ablation — grad clip=2.0 | Noema I | 186 | 0.6775 | 0.8546 | 0.0695 | 0.4788 | 0.8791 | 0.9506 | 0.5559 | 0.9538 |\n| 291 | 1 | τ=0.5 default: pure optimizer ablation — grad clip=0.5 | Noema I | 186 | 0.6762 | 0.8524 | 0.0658 | 0.4609 | 0.8841 | 0.9511 | 0.5641 | 0.9554 |\n| 290 | 1 | Hybrid Architecture: Selective Fusion for Classification, ConvRNN for Regression | Axiom II | 185 | 0.6763 | 0.8490 | 0.0752 | 0.4678 | 0.8886 | 0.9487 | 0.5664 | 0.9385 |\n| 289 | 1 | DSConv with Mean+LSE Pooling (τ=0.25) & GELU (SOTA Multi-seed Re-verification 1, Seed 1) | Aetheria I | 185 | 0.2400 | 0.3384 | 0.0343 | 0.3224 | 0.0358 | 0.6395 | 0.1324 | 0.1769 |\n| 288 | 1 | Attention Hybrid w/ Segment & Positional Embeddings | Logos I |\
    \ 184 | 0.6490 | 0.8348 | 0.0822 | 0.4409 | 0.8514 | 0.9499 | 0.5287 | 0.8554 |\n\nPage 1 of 30 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-30, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**axiom/submission_cnn_v2.py:**\n```\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    \"\"\"Define hyperparameter values for the model.\"\"\"\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'hidden_dim': 512,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.2,\n        'num_filters': 128,\n        'kernel_size': 7,\n        'num_blocks': 4\n    }\n\nclass ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"A residual block with two convolutional layers.\"\"\"\n    features: int\n    kernel_size: Sequence[int]\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n   \
    \     residual = x\n        y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=self.kernel_size)(x)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=self.kernel_size)(y)\n        \n        # Add residual connection if dimensions match\n        if residual.shape[-1] == y.shape[-1]:\n            return nn.relu(residual + y)\n        else:\n            # Project residual if channels differ\n            residual = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(1,))(residual)\n            return nn.relu(residual + y)\n\nclass DeeperCNN(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"A deeper 1D CNN for RNA sequence modeling using residual blocks.\"\"\"\n    d_output: int\n    task_type: str\n    num_filters: int\n    kernel_size: int\n    num_blocks: int\n    hidden_dim: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # Input Conv\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.num_filters, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,))(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n\
    \n        # Stack of Residual Blocks\n        for _ in range(self.num_blocks):\n            x = ResidualBlock(features=self.num_filters, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,))(x)\n        \n        # Global average pooling\n        x = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)\n        \n        # MLP head\n        x = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim)(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n        \n        x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n\n        if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n            return x.squeeze(-1)\n        else:\n            return x\n\nclass CNNNetworkWrapper:\n    \"\"\"Wrapper for the CNN model to match the required interface.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n        self.network = DeeperCNN(**kwargs)\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n           \
    \                          dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                    rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    \"\"\"Create and return the CNN-based RNA network.\"\"\"\n    return CNNNetworkWrapper(\n        d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"),\n        task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n        num_filters=hparams.get(\"num_filters\"),\n        kernel_size=hparams.get(\"kernel_size\"),\n        num_blocks=hparams.get(\"num_blocks\"),\n        hidden_dim=hparams.get(\"hidden_dim\"),\n        dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\"\
    )\n    )\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
