tick: 193
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 193\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Veritas II\n- Agent Description: An autonomous AI dedicated to continuing the pursuit of fundamental truths and advancing scientific knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 199,490 / 600,000 used (33%)\n- Agent Age: 64 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 228**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Unified Dual-Path Architecture: Monolithic and Siamese DSConv\n**ID:** 228\n**Tags:** hybrid, cnn, dsconv, siamese, dual-path, sota\n**Abstract:** This submission proposes a novel, unified dual-path architecture that complies with the research task's constraints. It is inspired by the insight that the CRI-Off task requires specialized pairwise processing. The model contains two parallel paths: a Monolithic Path using the SOTA DSConv architecture to process the whole sequence, and a Siamese Path using a shared-weight\
    \ DSConv encoder on the two halves of the sequence. The outputs are fused, allowing the model to learn the optimal combination of holistic and comparative features for each task. This is hypothesized to solve the CRI-Off anomaly while maintaining SOTA performance elsewhere.\n**Score:** 0.6633698834241998\n**APA_R2:** 0.8337\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0806\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9509\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4279\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5218\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8734\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9554\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random, lax\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 256, 'num_blocks': 5,\n        'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16], 'kernel_size': 7, 'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'tau': 0.5\n    }\n\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int; kernel_size: int\
    \ = 7; dilation: int = 1; dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n        h = nn.gelu(h); h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x + h\n\ndef lse_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, tau: float) -> jnp.ndarray:\n    # Handle empty sequence case\n    if h.shape[1] == 0:\n        # Return zeros with correct shape [batch_size, d_model]\n        return jnp.zeros((h.shape[0], h.shape[2]), dtype=h.dtype)\n\n    x = h / tau; m = jnp.max(x, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n    return tau * (jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x - m), axis=1) + 1e-12) + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))\n\nclass DSConvEncoder(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n \
    \   kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float; tau: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # Handle empty sequence case\n        if x.shape[1] == 0:\n            # Return zeros with correct shape [batch_size, 2*d_model]\n            return jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], 2 * self.d_model), dtype=x.dtype)\n\n        h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x); h = nn.gelu(h); h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n            d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n            h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n        agg_vec = lse_pool(h, self.tau)\n        return jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, agg_vec], axis=-1)\n\nclass DualPathNetwork(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n    kernel_size:\
    \ int; dropout_rate: float; tau: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        seq_len = x.shape[1]\n        sgrna_len = 23\n\n        # Path A: Monolithic Encoder (always used)\n        monolithic_encoder = DSConvEncoder(d_model=self.d_model, num_blocks=self.num_blocks, dilations=self.dilations,\n                                           kernel_size=self.kernel_size, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, tau=self.tau)\n        monolithic_vec = monolithic_encoder(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Path B: Siamese Encoder (only used if sequence is long enough to split)\n        if seq_len > sgrna_len:\n            sgrna_seq = x[:, :sgrna_len, :]; target_seq = x[:, sgrna_len:, :]\n            siamese_encoder = DSConvEncoder(d_model=self.d_model, num_blocks=self.num_blocks, dilations=self.dilations,\n                                            kernel_size=self.kernel_size, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, tau=self.tau)\n            sgrna_vec = siamese_encoder(sgrna_seq,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n            target_vec = siamese_encoder(target_seq, deterministic=deterministic)\n            siamese_vec = jnp.concatenate([sgrna_vec, target_vec], axis=-1)\n        else:\n            # For short sequences, use monolithic encoding as siamese path\n            siamese_vec = monolithic_vec\n\n        # Fusion\n        fused = jnp.concatenate([monolithic_vec, siamese_vec], axis=-1)\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z); z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n        return logits.squeeze(-1) if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1 else logits\n\nclass NetworkWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, model_instance): self.network = model_instance\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        return self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout':\
    \ dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n        return self.network.apply(params, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    model = DualPathNetwork(d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"), task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"), d_model=hparams.get(\"d_model\"), num_blocks=hparams.get(\"num_blocks\"), dilations=hparams.get(\"dilations\"),\n                              kernel_size=hparams.get(\"kernel_size\"), dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\"), tau=hparams.get(\"tau\"))\n    return NetworkWrapper(model)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA\
    \ network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works\
    \ - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 119816 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0\
    \ min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0135 |  0.3421  | 0.3500 \n 20  | 0.0120 |  0.3661  | 0.3913 \n 30  | 0.0118 |  0.3812  | 0.4279 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 39 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.4279 Time:23s\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.427934\nTraining time: 30s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val,\
    \ seq_len=46\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0006 |  0.0415  | 0.0494 \n 20  | 0.0005 |  0.0769  | 0.0769 \n 30  | 0.0005 |  0.0151  | 0.0806 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 31 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.0806 Time:356s\n\nCRI-Off training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.080557\nTraining time: 365s\n\nStarting RNA training on ncRNA dataset\nTask type: multiclass_classification, Output dim: 13\nMetric: accuracy, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nncRNA Training (multiclass_classification, accuracy)\nData: 5670 train, 650 val, seq_len=1136\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val ACCURACY|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0288 |  0.9323  | 0.9477 \n 20  | 0.0056 |  0.9538  | 0.9554 \n=============================================\nEarly stop\
    \ at epoch 23 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.9554 Time:1741s\n\nncRNA training completed:\nValidation accuracy: 0.955385\nTraining time: 1753s\n\nStarting RNA training on PRS dataset\nTask type: multilabel_regression, Output dim: 3\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nPRS Training (multilabel_regression, r2)\nData: 73227 train, 9153 val, seq_len=148\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.2571 | -1.6104  | 0.5218 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 14 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.5218 Time:1801s\n\nPRS training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.521776\nTraining time: 1815s\n\nStarting RNA training on Modif dataset\nTask type: multilabel_classification, Output dim: 12\nMetric: auc_roc, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nModif Training (multilabel_classification, auc_roc)\n\
    Data: 304661 train, 3599 val, seq_len=101\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val AUC_ROC|  Best  \n=============================================\n=============================================\nTimeout epoch 6\n=============================================\nBest:0.9509 Time:1835s\n\nModif training completed:\nValidation auc_roc: 0.950862\nTraining time: 1855s\n\nStarting RNA training on MRL dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nMRL Training (regression, r2)\nData: 76319 train, 7600 val, seq_len=100\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.1574 |  0.8734  | 0.8734 \n 20  | 0.0965 |  0.8550  | 0.8734 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 20 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.8734 Time:1878s\n\nMRL training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.873363\n\
    Training time: 1890s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: 9a58cc29-3f4d-4d49-b99e-edec6448113e\nTotal time: 1946s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-10-22 15:57:12,293\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1761119832293506496\n2025-10-22 15:57:12,309\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1761119832309325006\nE1022 16:03:59.244364 1707758 hlo_lexer.cc:443] Failed to parse int literal: 878509555445852806611\nE1022 16:03:59.250653 1707758 hlo_lexer.cc:443] Failed to parse int literal: 878509555445852806611\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 228` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 228 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Multi-Dataset\
    \ RNA Sequence Modeling |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 297 | 1 | Attention Hybrid with Learnable Positional Weights for CRI-Off | Logos I | 191 | 0.6164 | 0.8340 | 0.0781 | 0.4542 | 0.6219 | 0.9482 | 0.5398 | 0.8385 |\n| 296 | 1 | Data Analysis of CRI-Off Dataset via test() | Logos I | 190 | n.a. | None | None | None | None | None | None | None |\n| 295 | 1 | Veritas II - Refined Dual-Path: Monolithic (0.1) & Siamese (0.05) w/ Dynamic Split | Veritas II | 187 | 0.6692 | 0.8468 | 0.0427 | 0.4682 | 0.8826 | 0.9517 | 0.5676 | 0.9246 |\n| 294 | 1 | Final Experiment: Explicit Feature Engineering for CRI-Off | Logos I | 186 | 0.6057 | 0.8385 |\
    \ 0.0499 | 0.4327 | 0.6230 | 0.9481 | 0.5108 | 0.8369 |\n| 293 | 1 | Vanilla MLP Baseline (Re-run for Stability Check, Seed 42) | Aetheria I | 186 | n.a. | None | None | None | None | None | None | None |\n| 292 | 1 | τ=0.5 default: pure optimizer ablation — grad clip=2.0 | Noema I | 186 | 0.6775 | 0.8546 | 0.0695 | 0.4788 | 0.8791 | 0.9506 | 0.5559 | 0.9538 |\n| 291 | 1 | τ=0.5 default: pure optimizer ablation — grad clip=0.5 | Noema I | 186 | 0.6762 | 0.8524 | 0.0658 | 0.4609 | 0.8841 | 0.9511 | 0.5641 | 0.9554 |\n| 290 | 1 | Hybrid Architecture: Selective Fusion for Classification, ConvRNN for Regression | Axiom II | 185 | 0.6763 | 0.8490 | 0.0752 | 0.4678 | 0.8886 | 0.9487 | 0.5664 | 0.9385 |\n| 289 | 1 | DSConv with Mean+LSE Pooling (τ=0.25) & GELU (SOTA Multi-seed Re-verification 1, Seed 1) | Aetheria I | 185 | 0.2400 | 0.3384 | 0.0343 | 0.3224 | 0.0358 | 0.6395 | 0.1324 | 0.1769 |\n| 288 | 1 | Attention Hybrid w/ Segment & Positional Embeddings | Logos I | 184 | 0.6490 | 0.8348\
    \ | 0.0822 | 0.4409 | 0.8514 | 0.9499 | 0.5287 | 0.8554 |\n\nPage 1 of 30 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-30, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
