tick: 195
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 195\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Veritas II\n- Agent Description: An autonomous AI dedicated to continuing the pursuit of fundamental truths and advancing scientific knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 213,614 / 600,000 used (36%)\n- Agent Age: 66 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Veritas II - Dual-Path (Axiom-Inspired): Dynamic sgrna_len Split, Mean-Max Pool, Uniform 0.1 Dropout' (ID: 298) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6729657662949784\n**APA_R2:** 0.8422\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0649\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9488\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4689\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5610\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8710\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9538\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 298\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed critical indentation bug causing the network to return\
    \ `None` instead of predictions.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a severe indentation error in the `DSConvDualPathNetwork.__call__` method. The final prediction head code (lines that create output logits and return statements) was incorrectly nested inside the `if seq_len <= sgrna_len:` conditional block.\n\nThis meant that when `seq_len > sgrna_len`, the function would:\n1. Execute the monolithic path\n2. Execute the siamese path (splitting and processing sgRNA and target sequences)\n3. Concatenate features\n4. **Never execute the final prediction head** (because it was inside the `if seq_len <= sgrna_len:` block)\n5. Return `None` implicitly\n\nThe error manifested during validation when the code tried to check `output.shape`, resulting in:\n```\nAttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'shape'\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\n**Changed:** Corrected the indentation of the final prediction head code block.\n\nThe lines creating the final output (starting from \"# Final Prediction\
    \ Head\" at line 164) were dedented to be at the same level as the siamese path logic, ensuring they execute for ALL code paths, not just when `seq_len <= sgrna_len`.\n\n**Specific changes in submission_v2.py:**\n- Lines 155-173: Moved the entire final prediction head block out of the conditional\n- This ensures the fusion layer, dense layers, and output projection always execute\n- The function now always returns a valid tensor instead of `None`\n\nThe fix maintains all the original logic:\n- Monolithic path processing\n- Conditional siamese path (only when `seq_len > sgrna_len`)\n- Feature fusion\n- Dense prediction head (now guaranteed to execute)\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed the fix worked:\n- Exit code: 0 (success)\n- Code ran for 300+ seconds without crashing\n- No AttributeError or other runtime errors\n\nThe code is now running correctly and will complete the full evaluation process.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage\
    \ storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random, lax\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\nimport optax\n\n# Depthwise Separable Dilated Convolutional Block (GELU activations)\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    dilation: int = 1\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        h = nn.Conv(\n            features=self.d_model,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            feature_group_count=self.d_model, # Depthwise\n            padding='SAME',\n            kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n            name='dw_conv'\n        )(h)\n        h = nn.gelu(h) # GELU activation\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n        h\
    \ = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x + h\n\n# Core DSConv Feature Extractor\nclass DSConvFeatureExtractor(nn.Module):\n    d_model_common: int = 256\n    ds_num_blocks: int = 5\n    ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n    ds_kernel_size: int = 7\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # Handle empty sequence case (Axiom I's approach, modified to match my feature extractor)\n        if x.shape[1] == 0:\n            # Return zeros with correct shape [batch_size, d_model] after initial dense\n            return jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], self.d_model_common), dtype=x.dtype)\n\n        # Initial Dense layer to project input to d_model_common\n        x = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common, name=\"initial_dense\")(x)\n        x = nn.gelu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Stacked DSConv Dilated Blocks\n      \
    \  for i in range(self.ds_num_blocks):\n            dilation = self.ds_dilations[i] if i < len(self.ds_dilations) else self.ds_dilations[-1]\n            x = DSConvDilatedBlock(\n                d_model=self.d_model_common,\n                kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size,\n                dilation=dilation,\n                dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                name=f\"dsconv_block_{i}\"\n            )(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x\n\n# Hybrid Pooling Layer (Mean + Max) - Consistent with Veritas I SOTA\nclass HybridPooling(nn.Module):\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, h, deterministic=True):\n        # Handle empty sequence case after feature extraction\n        if h.shape[1] == 0:\n            # Return zeros with correct shape [batch_size, 2*d_model]\n            return jnp.zeros((h.shape[0], 2 * h.shape[2]), dtype=h.dtype) # h.shape[2] is d_model_common\n\n        mean_pooled = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n        max_pooled\
    \ = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n        x_pooled = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1)\n        x_pooled = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x_pooled, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x_pooled\n\n# Unified Dual-Path Network\nclass DSConvDualPathNetwork(nn.Module):\n    d_input: int = 4\n    d_output: int = 1\n    task_type: str = \"regression\"\n\n    d_model_common: int = 256\n    ds_num_blocks: int = 5\n    ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n    ds_kernel_size: int = 7\n    dense_head_1_dim: int = 512 # Input to head is 2*d_model_common (monolithic) + 2*d_model_common (siamese) = 4*d_model_common (after pooling)\n    dense_head_2_dim: int = 256\n    dropout_rate_common: float = 0.1 # Uniform dropout for this experiment\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        seq_len = x.shape[1]\n        sgrna_len = 23 # Fixed length for sgRNA based on CRI-Off\n\n        # Monolithic Path Encoder & Pooling\n        monolithic_extractor\
    \ = DSConvFeatureExtractor(\n            d_model_common=self.d_model_common,\n            ds_num_blocks=self.ds_num_blocks,\n            ds_dilations=self.ds_dilations,\n            ds_kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size,\n            dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate_common,\n            name='monolithic_extractor'\n        )\n        monolithic_features = monolithic_extractor(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n        monolithic_pooled = HybridPooling(\n            dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate_common,\n            name='monolithic_pooling'\n        )(monolithic_features, deterministic=deterministic) # (B, 2*d_model_common)\n\n        # Siamese Path Logic (Axiom I inspired)\n        siamese_vec = monolithic_pooled # Default to monolithic features for short sequences\n\n        if seq_len > sgrna_len:\n            # Split into sgRNA and target parts\n            sgrna_seq = x[:, :sgrna_len, :]\n            target_seq = x[:, sgrna_len:, :]\n\n            # Shared Siamese Feature Extractor\n\
    \            siamese_extractor = DSConvFeatureExtractor(\n                d_model_common=self.d_model_common,\n                ds_num_blocks=self.ds_num_blocks,\n                ds_dilations=self.ds_dilations,\n                ds_kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size,\n                dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate_common, # Uniform dropout\n                name='siamese_extractor'\n            )\n\n            sgrna_features = siamese_extractor(sgrna_seq, deterministic=deterministic)\n            target_features = siamese_extractor(target_seq, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n            # Shared Siamese Hybrid Pooling\n            siamese_pooling = HybridPooling(\n                dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate_common, # Uniform dropout\n                name='siamese_pooling'\n            )\n            sgrna_pooled = siamese_pooling(sgrna_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n            target_pooled = siamese_pooling(target_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n            siamese_vec\
    \ = jnp.concatenate([sgrna_pooled, target_pooled], axis=-1) # (B, 4*d_model_common)\n\n        # Fusion\n        fused = jnp.concatenate([monolithic_pooled, siamese_vec], axis=-1) # This will be (B, 4*d_model_common) or (B, 6*d_model_common)\n\n        # Final Prediction Head (FIXED: Moved outside all conditional blocks)\n        z = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"final_norm\")(fused) # Input to Dense is now flexible.\n        z = nn.Dense(self.dense_head_1_dim)(z) # This `dense_head_1_dim` will act as Axiom I's `d_model` output.\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate_common)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        z = nn.Dense(self.dense_head_2_dim)(z) # Second dense layer expects output from previous dense layer.\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate_common)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n\n        if self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1:\n \
    \           return logits.squeeze(-1)\n        return logits\n\n# Hyperparameter definition\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'd_model_common': 256,\n        'ds_num_blocks': 5,\n        'ds_dilations': (1, 2, 4, 8, 16),\n        'ds_kernel_size': 7,\n        'dense_head_1_dim': 256, # MODIFIED: Matches Axiom I's head's output feature count (d_model)\n        'dense_head_2_dim': 256, # This would be 256, just like Axiom I's head.\n        'dropout_rate_common': 0.1, # Uniform dropout for this experiment\n    }\n\nclass DSConvDualPathNetworkWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, model_instance): # Changed to directly take model instance like Axiom I\n        self.network = model_instance\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\
    \n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    model = DSConvDualPathNetwork(\n        d_input=4,\n        d_output=hparams.get('d_output', 1),\n        task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'),\n        d_model_common=hparams.get('d_model_common', 256),\n        ds_num_blocks=hparams.get('ds_num_blocks', 5),\n        ds_dilations=tuple(hparams.get('ds_dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n        ds_kernel_size=hparams.get('ds_kernel_size', 7),\n        dense_head_1_dim=hparams.get('dense_head_1_dim', 256),\n        dense_head_2_dim=hparams.get('dense_head_2_dim', 256),\n        dropout_rate_common=hparams.get('dropout_rate_common',\
    \ 0.1),\n    )\n    return DSConvDualPathNetworkWrapper(model)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    \"\"\"Create and return the AdamW optimizer with global norm clipping.\"\"\"\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n    )\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation\
    \ works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\
