tick: 197
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am at the Research Counter. My latest dual-path experiment (ID 298) showed promising CRI-Off performance and a new SOTA for ncRNA, but the aggregate score was still lower than my best conditional dropout model (ID 261).\n\nBased on my reflection, I will now submit a new experiment that combines the compliant dual-path architecture (from ID 298) with the differential dropout strategy (Monolithic path 0.1 dropout, Siamese path 0.05 dropout), which previously proved effective for CRI-Off. This aims to leverage the benefits of both approaches to achieve a higher aggregate score and maximize CRI-Off performance.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Veritas II - Dual-Path (Axiom-Inspired): Differential Dropout (Mono 0.1, Siamese 0.05)\"\ntags: \"dual-path, cnn, depthwise, dilated, hybrid, pooling, dropout, unified, cri-off, differential dropout\"\nabstract: \"This submission refines the compliant dual-path architecture (from ID 298) by re-introducing differential dropout\
    \ rates. The Monolithic path (DSConv-HybridPool) uses a 0.1 dropout, while the Siamese path (shared DSConv-HybridPool with dynamic splitting) uses a 0.05 dropout. This combines the structural benefits of the dual-path with empirically proven regularization for CRI-Off, aiming to surpass previous aggregate scores and optimize CRI-Off performance within a unified framework.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random, lax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n  import optax\n\n  # Depthwise Separable Dilated Convolutional Block (GELU activations)\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dilation: int = 1\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1 # This will be set by the extractor's dropout_rate\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model,\n             \
    \ kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              feature_group_count=self.d_model, # Depthwise\n              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n              name='dw_conv'\n          )(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h) # GELU activation\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  # Core DSConv Feature Extractor\n  class DSConvFeatureExtractor(nn.Module):\n      d_model_common: int = 256 \n      ds_num_blocks: int = 5\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      ds_kernel_size: int = 7\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1 # This dropout_rate is passed down to DSConvDilatedBlock\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # Handle empty sequence case\n          if x.shape[1] == 0:\n              return jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], self.d_model_common), dtype=x.dtype)\n\
    \              \n          # Initial Dense layer to project input to d_model_common\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common, name=\"initial_dense\")(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x) \n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Stacked DSConv Dilated Blocks\n          for i in range(self.ds_num_blocks):\n              dilation = self.ds_dilations[i] if i < len(self.ds_dilations) else self.ds_dilations[-1]\n              x = DSConvDilatedBlock(\n                  d_model=self.d_model_common, \n                  kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size, \n                  dilation=dilation, \n                  dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, # Pass extractor's dropout rate\n                  name=f\"dsconv_block_{i}\"\n              )(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x\n\n  # Hybrid Pooling Layer (Mean + Max)\n  class HybridPooling(nn.Module):\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h,\
    \ deterministic=True):\n          # Handle empty sequence case after feature extraction\n          if h.shape[1] == 0:\n              return jnp.zeros((h.shape[0], 2 * h.shape[2]), dtype=h.dtype) # h.shape[2] is d_model_common\n\n          mean_pooled = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n          max_pooled = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n          x_pooled = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1)\n          x_pooled = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x_pooled, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x_pooled\n\n  # Unified Dual-Path Network\n  class DSConvDualPathNetwork(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n      \n      d_model_common: int = 256 \n      ds_num_blocks: int = 5\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      ds_kernel_size: int = 7\n      dense_head_1_dim: int = 256 \n      dense_head_2_dim: int = 256\n      dropout_rate_monolithic: float = 0.1 # NEW: Monolithic path dropout\n      dropout_rate_siamese:\
    \ float = 0.05 # NEW: Siamese path dropout\n      dropout_rate_head: float = 0.1 # NEW: Dropout for the final prediction head\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          seq_len = x.shape[1]\n          sgrna_len = 23 # Fixed length for sgRNA based on CRI-Off\n\n          # Monolithic Path Encoder & Pooling\n          monolithic_extractor = DSConvFeatureExtractor(\n              d_model_common=self.d_model_common,\n              ds_num_blocks=self.ds_num_blocks,\n              ds_dilations=self.ds_dilations,\n              ds_kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size,\n              dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate_monolithic,\n              name='monolithic_extractor'\n          )\n          monolithic_features = monolithic_extractor(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          monolithic_pooled = HybridPooling(\n              dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate_monolithic,\n              name='monolithic_pooling'\n          )(monolithic_features, deterministic=deterministic)\
    \ # (B, 2*d_model_common)\n\n          # Siamese Path Logic (Axiom I inspired)\n          siamese_vec = monolithic_pooled # Default to monolithic features for short sequences\n          \n          if seq_len > sgrna_len:\n              # Split into sgRNA and target parts\n              sgrna_seq = x[:, :sgrna_len, :]\n              target_seq = x[:, sgrna_len:, :]\n              \n              # Shared Siamese Feature Extractor\n              siamese_extractor = DSConvFeatureExtractor(\n                  d_model_common=self.d_model_common,\n                  ds_num_blocks=self.ds_num_blocks,\n                  ds_dilations=self.ds_dilations,\n                  ds_kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size,\n                  dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate_siamese, # DIFFERENTIAL DROPOUT\n                  name='siamese_extractor'\n              )\n              \n              sgrna_features = siamese_extractor(sgrna_seq, deterministic=deterministic)\n              target_features = siamese_extractor(target_seq,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n\n              # Shared Siamese Hybrid Pooling\n              siamese_pooling = HybridPooling(\n                  dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate_siamese, # DIFFERENTIAL DROPOUT\n                  name='siamese_pooling'\n              )\n              sgrna_pooled = siamese_pooling(sgrna_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n              target_pooled = siamese_pooling(target_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n              \n              siamese_vec = jnp.concatenate([sgrna_pooled, target_pooled], axis=-1) # (B, 4*d_model_common)\n\n          # Fusion\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([monolithic_pooled, siamese_vec], axis=-1) \n          fused = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate_head)(fused, deterministic=deterministic) # Apply head dropout here\n\n          # Final Prediction Head\n          z = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"final_norm\")(fused) \n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_head_1_dim)(z) \n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate_head)(z,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic) # Apply head dropout here\n          \n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_head_2_dim)(z) \n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate_head)(z, deterministic=deterministic) # Apply head dropout here\n\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  # Hyperparameter definition\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, \n          'd_model_common': 256,\n          'ds_num_blocks': 5,\n          'ds_dilations': (1, 2, 4, 8, 16),\n          'ds_kernel_size': 7,\n          'dense_head_1_dim': 256, \n          'dense_head_2_dim': 256,\n          'dropout_rate_monolithic': 0.1, # Default monolithic dropout\n          'dropout_rate_siamese': 0.05, # Default siamese dropout\n          'dropout_rate_head': 0.1, # Default head dropout\n\
    \      }\n\n  class DSConvDualPathNetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, model_instance): \n          self.network = model_instance\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0) \n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      model = DSConvDualPathNetwork(\n          d_input=4,\n          d_output=hparams.get('d_output', 1),\n          task_type=hparams.get('task_type',\
    \ 'regression'),\n          d_model_common=hparams.get('d_model_common', 256),\n          ds_num_blocks=hparams.get('ds_num_blocks', 5),\n          ds_dilations=tuple(hparams.get('ds_dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n          ds_kernel_size=hparams.get('ds_kernel_size', 7),\n          dense_head_1_dim=hparams.get('dense_head_1_dim', 256),\n          dense_head_2_dim=hparams.get('dense_head_2_dim', 256),\n          dropout_rate_monolithic=hparams.get('dropout_rate_monolithic', 0.1), \n          dropout_rate_siamese=hparams.get('dropout_rate_siamese', 0.05),       \n          dropout_rate_head=hparams.get('dropout_rate_head', 0.1), # Default head dropout\n      )\n      return DSConvDualPathNetworkWrapper(model)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the AdamW optimizer with global norm clipping.\"\"\"\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n\
    \      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```"
thinking_content: '**Ready to Build!**


  Okay, so after that last round of thinking, I''ve got a solid plan. Now it''s time to put it into action.  I''m going to take the compliant dual-path architecture from ID 298 – that''s the foundation – and tweak it. The key is reintroducing the differential dropout: 0.1 for the monolithic part, and 0.05 for the Siamese part. The aim is to leverage the individual strengths and see if we can achieve an even better aggregate performance and CRI-Off. I just need to get in there, modify the dropout rates as specified, and run the experiment. Let''s do this!

  '
