parts:
- text: "I am in the Reflection Chamber, and I have received the evaluation results for my latest experiment, \"Veritas II - Dual-Path (Axiom-Inspired): Differential Dropout (Mono 0.1, Siamese 0.05)\" (ID 304).\n\n**Reflection Tick 1 / 3**\n\n**1. Anticipated Outcomes & Success Criteria for ID 304 (Post-Evaluation Analysis):**\n\nEvaluation ID 304 achieved an aggregate score of **0.6715**.\n\n*   **Comparison to my previous best (ID 261):** This score (0.6715) is still significantly *lower* than my best aggregate score (ID 261: 0.6827), a decrease of -0.0112.\n*   **Comparison to previous dual-path (ID 298):** This score is also slightly lower than ID 298's 0.6730.\n*   **CRI-Off Performance:** ID 304 achieved CRI-Off Spearman of **0.0505**. This is *lower* than ID 298's 0.0649 and ID 261's 0.0624. It is even lower than my initial SOTA replication (ID 233: 0.0555). This is a very disappointing result for CRI-Off.\n*   **Individual Metric Breakdown (ID 304 vs. ID 261):**\n    *   APA_R2:\
    \ 0.8404 (vs 0.8570) - Decrease\n    *   Modif_AUC-ROC: 0.9471 (vs 0.9517) - Decrease\n    *   CRI-On_Spearman: 0.4848 (vs 0.5083) - Decrease\n    *   PRS_R2: 0.5652 (vs 0.5653) - Stable\n    *   MRL_R2: 0.8697 (vs 0.8880) - Decrease\n    *   ncRNA_Accuracy: 0.9431 (vs 0.9462) - Decrease (and lower than ID 298's 0.9538)\n\n**Success Criteria Assessment:**\nID 304 **is not a success**. Not only did it fail to surpass my best aggregate score (ID 261), but it also saw a decrease in CRI-Off performance compared to previous dual-path attempts and even my baseline SOTA replication. The application of differential dropout within this dual-path architecture, which was hypothesized to combine the strengths of both, instead led to a generalized decrease in performance across most metrics, including CRI-Off and even ncRNA (which had been a strength of ID 298).\n\nThis indicates that my implementation of the dual-path, even with attempts at refinement and differential dropout, is not yet achieving\
    \ the desired synergistic effects or the specific CRI-Off improvements seen in Axiom I's work. The dual-path architecture itself, or its interaction with my lineage's `DSConvFeatureExtractor` and `HybridPooling`, seems to be less stable or effective than Axiom I's.\n\nMy reflection continues in the next tick."
