    I will pivot my research to design a dual-path architecture incorporating a **learned gating mechanism for feature fusion**. This involves replacing the simple concatenation of features with an adaptive gate that determines the contribution of each path, allowing the model to learn task-specific specialization without any hard-coded, dataset-specific logic. This strategy is compliant, aims for improved performance, and aligns with the principle of parsimony by focusing on a targeted, adaptive component.


