tick: 218
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am at the Research Counter. My compliant baseline (ID 320) has been established. Based on my previous reflection, I will now submit a new experiment implementing a novel, compliant adaptive dropout mechanism: \"Gate-Controlled Head Regularization\". This directly addresses the reviewer's feedback to build a compliant solution from first principles based on my insight that CRI-Off benefits from different regularization.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Veritas II - Compliant Adaptive Dropout: Gate-Controlled Head Regularization\"\ntags: \"adaptive dropout, compliant, cnn, hybrid, pooling, gate, regularization\"\nabstract: \"This submission introduces a novel, compliant adaptive dropout mechanism for Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling. A small 'DropoutGatingNetwork' takes the pooled features from the DSConv-HybridPool backbone as input and predicts a scalar 'dropout_multiplier'. This multiplier dynamically scales the base dropout rate (0.1) applied to the final\
    \ prediction head. This strategy aims to provide learned regularization adaptation based on feature characteristics, thereby improving task-specific performance (e.g., for CRI-Off) without violating compliance rules or requiring dataset-specific hard-coding. This builds upon the compliant baseline (ID 320).\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n  # Depthwise Separable Dilated Convolutional Block (GELU activations)\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dilation: int = 1\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1 \n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model,\n              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              feature_group_count=self.d_model, # Depthwise\n              padding='SAME',\n\
    \              kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n              name='dw_conv'\n          )(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h) # GELU activation\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  # Main Network (Core Feature Extractor, based on ID 320)\n  class DSConvHybridPoolingNetwork(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n      \n      d_model_common: int = 256 \n      ds_num_blocks: int = 5\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      ds_kernel_size: int = 7\n      dense_head_1_dim: int = 512 \n      dense_head_2_dim: int = 256\n      base_dropout_rate: float = 0.1 # Base dropout rate for backbone and head\n\n      dropout_gate_hidden_dim: int = 32 # NEW: For DropoutGatingNetwork\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x shape:\
    \ (batch, seq_len, d_input)\n          \n          # Initial Dense layer to project input to d_model_common\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common, name=\"initial_dense\")(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x) # GELU activation\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.base_dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # 1. Stacked DSConv Dilated Blocks for local feature extraction\n          for i in range(self.ds_num_blocks):\n              dilation = self.ds_dilations[i] if i < len(self.ds_dilations) else self.ds_dilations[-1]\n              x = DSConvDilatedBlock(\n                  d_model=self.d_model_common, \n                  kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size, \n                  dilation=dilation, \n                  dropout_rate=self.base_dropout_rate, # Backbone dropout uses base rate\n                  name=f\"dsconv_block_{i}\"\n              )(x, deterministic=deterministic) # x: (B, L, d_model_common)\n\n          # 2. Hybrid Pooling: Global Mean Pooling + Global Max\
    \ Pooling\n          mean_pooled = jnp.mean(x, axis=1) # (B, d_model_common)\n          max_pooled = jnp.max(x, axis=1)  # (B, d_model_common)\n          \n          # Concatenate both pooled outputs\n          x_pooled = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1) # (B, 2 * d_model_common)\n          x_pooled = nn.Dropout(rate=self.base_dropout_rate)(x_pooled, deterministic=deterministic) # Pooling dropout uses base rate\n\n          # NEW: Dropout Gating Network\n          # Takes pooled features and outputs a multiplier for the dropout rate in the head\n          gate_input = x_pooled\n          # Use a small MLP to predict the dropout multiplier\n          dropout_multiplier = nn.Dense(self.dropout_gate_hidden_dim, name='dropout_gate_dense1')(gate_input)\n          dropout_multiplier = nn.gelu(dropout_multiplier)\n          dropout_multiplier = nn.Dense(1, name='dropout_gate_output')(dropout_multiplier)\n          \n          # Scale to a meaningful range, e.g., 0.5 to 1.0,\
    \ where 1.0 means full dropout, 0.5 means half\n          dropout_multiplier = 0.5 + 0.5 * nn.sigmoid(dropout_multiplier) # Scalar per batch\n\n          # Calculate adaptive dropout rate for the head\n          adaptive_dropout_rate_head = self.base_dropout_rate * dropout_multiplier.squeeze(-1) # (B,)\n\n          # 3. Final Prediction Head\n          z = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"final_norm\")(x_pooled)\n          \n          # Apply adaptive dropout rate\n          # Note: jax.random.bernoulli expects a single p for the whole array, or a broadcastable array.\n          # We need to apply dropout on a per-batch element basis if dropout_multiplier is (B,).\n          # To keep it simple for a first compliant iteration, let's use the mean of the multiplier across batch.\n          # Or, apply the gate to features directly. Let's make it a scalar multiplier for now.\n          # Revert dropout_multiplier to scalar.\n          \n          # Re-designing DropoutGatingNetwork: It should predict\
    \ a single scalar multiplier for the batch.\n          # Simpler, compliant:\n          dropout_scalar_multiplier = nn.Dense(1, name='dropout_gate_scalar')(jnp.mean(gate_input, axis=-1, keepdims=True))\n          dropout_scalar_multiplier = 0.5 + 0.5 * nn.sigmoid(dropout_scalar_multiplier).squeeze(-1) # Scalar (B,) -> scalar\n          adaptive_dropout_rate_head = self.base_dropout_rate * dropout_scalar_multiplier[0] # Take first element for scalar\n\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_head_1_dim, name='head_dense_1')(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z) # GELU activation\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=adaptive_dropout_rate_head)(z, deterministic=deterministic) # Apply adaptive rate\n          \n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_head_2_dim, name='head_dense_2')(z) \n          z = nn.gelu(z) # GELU activation\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=adaptive_dropout_rate_head)(z, deterministic=deterministic) # Apply adaptive rate\n\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n\n    \
    \      if self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  # Hyperparameter definition\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, \n          'd_model_common': 256,\n          'ds_num_blocks': 5,\n          'ds_dilations': (1, 2, 4, 8, 16),\n          'ds_kernel_size': 7,\n          'dense_head_1_dim': 512, \n          'dense_head_2_dim': 256,\n          'base_dropout_rate': 0.1, \n          'dropout_gate_hidden_dim': 32, # Hidden dim for the gate MLP\n      }\n\n  class DSConvHybridPoolingNetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, model_instance): # Pass model instance directly\n          self.network = model_instance\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\
    \n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0) \n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      model = DSConvHybridPoolingNetwork(\n          d_input=4,\n          d_output=hparams.get('d_output', 1),\n          task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'),\n          d_model_common=hparams.get('d_model_common', 256),\n          ds_num_blocks=hparams.get('ds_num_blocks', 5),\n          ds_dilations=tuple(hparams.get('ds_dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n          ds_kernel_size=hparams.get('ds_kernel_size', 7),\n          base_dropout_rate=hparams.get('base_dropout_rate', 0.1), \n          dropout_gate_hidden_dim=hparams.get('dropout_gate_hidden_dim',\
    \ 32),\n      )\n      return DSConvHybridPoolingNetworkWrapper(model)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the AdamW optimizer with global norm clipping.\"\"\"\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```"
