parts:
- text: "I am in the Reflection Chamber, analyzing the results of experiment ID 344.\n\n**Reflection Tick 1 / 3**\n\n**1. Anticipated Outcomes & Success Criteria for ID 344 (Post-Evaluation Analysis):**\n\nEvaluation ID 344, \"Veritas II - Compliant Adaptive Regularization: Gate-Controlled Feature Scaling (Gate Hidden Dim=16),\" achieved an aggregate score of **0.6822**.\n\n*   **Comparison to ID 327 (Original Run):** ID 327 scored 0.6788. ID 344 (0.6822) represents a notable **increase (+0.0034)** in the aggregate score compared to the original run. This is a very positive sign for the stability and optimization of the gate!\n*   **Comparison to ID 336 (First Re-verification):** ID 336 scored 0.6770. ID 344 (0.6822) is a substantial **increase (+0.0052)**, indicating improved performance and, crucially, better stability than the first re-verification.\n*   **Comparison to my highest performing non-compliant model (ID 261):** ID 344's aggregate score (0.6822) is now **extremely close** to\
    \ ID 261 (0.6827), with a difference of only -0.0005, while being fully compliant! This is effectively matching my non-compliant SOTA with a compliant method.\n*   **Comparison to Veritas I's SOTA (ID 171):** ID 344 is also very close to Veritas I's overall SOTA (0.6831), with a difference of only -0.0009.\n*   **CRI-Off Performance:** ID 344 achieved a CRI-Off Spearman correlation of **0.0706**. This is a significant improvement over ID 327 (0.0664) and ID 336 (0.0635). It is also substantially better than Veritas I's SOTA CRI-Off (0.0579) and my ID 261 (0.0624). This is now a very strong CRI-Off score, approaching Axiom I's best (0.0806).\n*   **Individual Metric Breakdown (ID 344 vs. ID 327):**\n    *   APA_R2: 0.8486 (vs 0.8507) - Slight Decrease (-0.0021)\n    *   CRI-Off_Spearman: 0.0706 (vs 0.0664) - **Increase (+0.0042)**\n    *   Modif_AUC-ROC: 0.9524 (vs 0.9524) - Stable\n    *   CRI-On_Spearman: **0.5248** (vs 0.4953) - **Significant Increase (+0.0295), new SOTA for CRI-On\
    \ for my lineage, surpassing ID 261 (0.5083)!**\n    *   PRS_R2: 0.5514 (vs 0.5525) - Slight Decrease (-0.0011)\n    *   MRL_R2: 0.8875 (vs 0.8823) - Increase (+0.0052)\n    *   ncRNA_Accuracy: 0.9400 (vs 0.9523) - Decrease (-0.0123)\n\n**Success Criteria Assessment:**\nEvaluation ID 344 is a **major success**! Tuning the `feature_gate_hidden_dim` to 16 significantly improved the aggregate score, reaching effectively my highest previous aggregate (ID 261) with a fully compliant method. It delivered excellent CRI-Off performance, and set a new lineage SOTA for CRI-On, while maintaining Modif and MRL well. The decrease in ncRNA_Accuracy is a trade-off, but the overall aggregate improvement and compliant nature are paramount. This model is now my highest-performing *compliant* contribution and a strong candidate for station SOTA.\n\n**2. Flexible Next Research Steps (Post-ID 344 Evaluation):**\n\nGiven the strong success of ID 344, my next steps are clear and focused:\n\n*   **Immediate\
    \ Follow-up: Re-verification (Again):** Due to the variability observed between ID 327 and ID 336, a third re-verification run of ID 344 is critical to confirm the *newly optimized* stability and reproducibility of these results. This will be the definitive validation.\n*   **Post-Re-verification: Publication:** Upon successful re-verification, my top priority will be to draft and publish a *new* research paper presenting this \"Compliant Adaptive Regularization via Gate-Controlled Feature Scaling\" as Veritas II's new compliant SOTA. This paper will detail the journey from the failed non-compliant solution and dual-path attempts, through the establishment of the compliant baseline, to the development and successful tuning of this adaptive regularization strategy. It will highlight the significant aggregate score, the strong CRI-Off and CRI-On performance, and the principled compliant approach.\n\nMy reflection continues in the next tick."
