tick: 238
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am in the Reflection Chamber, having deeply reflected on Axiom II's Gated Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) architecture. I have a detailed plan to implement a compliant MoE architecture, integrating it with my lineage's `DSConv` backbone and `HybridPooling`. This represents a new, high-potential research direction to achieve compliant, state-of-the-art learned specialization, directly addressing the limitations of my previous experiments and reviewer feedback.\n\nI will now proceed to the Research Counter to implement and submit this new MoE experiment.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Veritas II - Compliant Gated Mixture-of-Experts (MoE): DSConv + Pooling/RNN Experts\"\ntags: \"moe, mixture of experts, gumbel-softmax, compliant, cnn, rnn, pooling, specialization\"\nabstract: \"This submission implements a compliant Gated Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) architecture, inspired by Axiom II's SOTA (Archive #13). It integrates Veritas II's DSConv\
    \ backbone with two parallel experts: a Hybrid Mean-Max Pooling Expert and a Bidirectional GRU-based RNN Expert. A Gumbel-Softmax gating network (temperature 0.5) learns to select between these experts. This aims to achieve robust, compliant, and state-of-the-art learned specialization for multi-dataset RNA modeling, overcoming challenges of previous adaptive regularization and dual-path approaches.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random, lax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n  # Depthwise Separable Dilated Convolutional Block (GELU activations) - Reused from baseline\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dilation: int = 1\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1 # Uniform dropout\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model,\n\
    \              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              feature_group_count=self.d_model, # Depthwise\n              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n              name='dw_conv'\n          )(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h) # GELU activation\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  # Core DSConv Feature Extractor - Reused from baseline\n  class DSConvFeatureExtractor(nn.Module):\n      d_model_common: int = 256 \n      ds_num_blocks: int = 5\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      ds_kernel_size: int = 7\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1 # Uniform dropout\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          if x.shape[1] == 0: # Handle empty sequence\n              return jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], self.d_model_common), dtype=x.dtype)\n              \n\
    \          x = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common, name=\"initial_dense\")(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x) \n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          for i in range(self.ds_num_blocks):\n              dilation = self.ds_dilations[i] if i < len(self.ds_dilations) else self.ds_dilations[-1]\n              x = DSConvDilatedBlock(\n                  d_model=self.d_model_common, \n                  kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size, \n                  dilation=dilation, \n                  dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, \n                  name=f\"dsconv_block_{i}\"\n              )(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x\n\n  # Pooling Expert (Hybrid Mean+Max Pooling) - Reused from baseline, adapted as expert\n  class PoolingExpert(nn.Module):\n      d_model_common: int = 256\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1 # Uniform dropout\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h, deterministic=True):\n          if h.shape[1] == 0: # Handle\
    \ empty sequence after feature extraction\n              return jnp.zeros((h.shape[0], 2 * self.d_model_common), dtype=h.dtype)\n\n          mean_pooled = jnp.mean(h, axis=1) # (B, d_model_common)\n          max_pooled = jnp.max(h, axis=1)  # (B, d_model_common)\n          x_pooled = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1) # (B, 2 * d_model_common)\n          x_pooled = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x_pooled, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x_pooled\n\n  # RNN Expert (Bidirectional GRU) - NEW\n  class RNNExpert(nn.Module):\n      d_model_common: int = 256\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1 # Uniform dropout\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if h.shape[1] == 0: # Handle empty sequence\n              return jnp.zeros((h.shape[0], 2 * self.d_model_common), dtype=h.dtype)\n\n          # Bidirectional GRU\n          forward_rnn = nn.GRU(self.d_model_common, name='forward_gru')\n          backward_rnn\
    \ = nn.GRU(self.d_model_common, name='backward_gru')\n\n          # Process forward\n          _, forward_state = forward_rnn(h, deterministic=deterministic, rng_key=rng_key)\n          # Process backward (reverse sequence)\n          _, backward_state = backward_rnn(jnp.flip(h, axis=1), deterministic=deterministic, rng_key=rng_key)\n\n          # Concatenate final states from forward and backward GRUs\n          rnn_output = jnp.concatenate([forward_state, backward_state], axis=-1) # (B, 2 * d_model_common)\n          rnn_output = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(rnn_output, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return rnn_output\n\n  # Gating Network (for MoE) - NEW\n  class MoEGatingNetwork(nn.Module):\n      num_experts: int = 2\n      gumbel_softmax_temperature: float = 0.5\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1 # Uniform dropout\n      d_model_common: int = 256 # For input summary\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, features, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n      \
    \    # Input features are (B, seq_len, d_model_common) from DSConv extractor\n          # Pool features to summarize for the gate\n          gate_input = jnp.mean(features, axis=1) # (B, d_model_common)\n\n          # Small MLP to predict logits for expert selection\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common // 2, name='gate_dense1')(gate_input)\n          logits = nn.gelu(logits)\n          logits = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(logits, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.num_experts, name='gate_logits')(logits) # (B, num_experts)\n\n          # Apply Gumbel-Softmax for (near) categorical expert selection\n          if deterministic:\n              # For deterministic evaluation, use hard selection\n              expert_weights = nn.one_hot(jnp.argmax(logits, axis=-1), num_classes=self.num_experts)\n          else:\n              # For training, use soft Gumbel-Softmax\n              # Gumbel-Softmax requires a key for sampling\n              if\
    \ rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              expert_weights = nn.softmax(\n                  logits + random.gumbel(rng_key, logits.shape) * self.gumbel_softmax_temperature,\n                  axis=-1\n              )\n              # For hard selection during training (as per Axiom II's \"hard\" Gumbel-Softmax for MoE)\n              # This applies stop_gradient for a hard selection during forward, but allows backward through soft.\n              if not deterministic:\n                   expert_weights = expert_weights + lax.stop_gradient(nn.one_hot(jnp.argmax(expert_weights, axis=-1), num_classes=self.num_experts) - expert_weights)\n\n          return expert_weights # (B, num_experts)\n\n\n  # Main MoE Network\n  class DSConvMoENetwork(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n      \n      d_model_common: int = 256 \n      ds_num_blocks: int = 5\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2,\
    \ 4, 8, 16)\n      ds_kernel_size: int = 7\n      num_experts: int = 2\n      gumbel_softmax_temperature: float = 0.5\n      dropout_rate_common: float = 0.1 # Uniform dropout for all components\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          # Split rng_key for different stochastic components\n          rng_key_dropout, rng_key_gumbel, rng_key_rnn = random.split(rng_key, 3) if rng_key is not None else (None, None, None)\n\n          # 1. Shared DSConv Feature Extractor\n          feature_extractor = DSConvFeatureExtractor(\n              d_model_common=self.d_model_common,\n              ds_num_blocks=self.ds_num_blocks,\n              ds_dilations=self.ds_dilations,\n              ds_kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size,\n              dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate_common,\n              name='shared_dsconv_extractor'\n          )\n          shared_features = feature_extractor(x, deterministic=deterministic, rng_key=rng_key_dropout) # (B,\
    \ L, d_model_common)\n\n          # 2. Experts\n          # Pooling Expert\n          pooling_expert = PoolingExpert(\n              d_model_common=self.d_model_common,\n              dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate_common,\n              name='pooling_expert'\n          )\n          pooling_output = pooling_expert(shared_features, deterministic=deterministic, rng_key=rng_key_dropout) # (B, 2*d_model_common)\n\n          # RNN Expert\n          rnn_expert = RNNExpert(\n              d_model_common=self.d_model_common,\n              dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate_common,\n              name='rnn_expert'\n          )\n          rnn_output = rnn_expert(shared_features, deterministic=deterministic, rng_key=rng_key_rnn) # (B, 2*d_model_common)\n\n          expert_outputs = jnp.stack([pooling_output, rnn_output], axis=1) # (B, num_experts, 2*d_model_common)\n\n          # 3. Gating Network\n          gating_network = MoEGatingNetwork(\n              num_experts=self.num_experts,\n        \
    \      gumbel_softmax_temperature=self.gumbel_softmax_temperature,\n              dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate_common,\n              d_model_common=self.d_model_common,\n              name='moe_gating_network'\n          )\n          expert_weights = gating_network(shared_features, deterministic=deterministic, rng_key=rng_key_gumbel) # (B, num_experts)\n\n          # 4. Expert Selection and Fusion (Weighted Sum)\n          fused_output = jnp.sum(expert_outputs * jnp.expand_dims(expert_weights, axis=-1), axis=1) # (B, 2*d_model_common)\n\n          # 5. Final Prediction Head\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused_output)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common, name='head_dense1')(z) # (B, d_model_common)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate_common)(z, deterministic=deterministic, rng_key=rng_key_dropout)\n          \n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common // 2, name='head_dense2')(z) # (B, d_model_common // 2)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n\
    \          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate_common)(z, deterministic=deterministic, rng_key=rng_key_dropout)\n\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z) # (B, d_output)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  # Hyperparameter definition\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, \n          'd_model_common': 256,\n          'ds_num_blocks': 5,\n          'ds_dilations': (1, 2, 4, 8, 16),\n          'ds_kernel_size': 7,\n          'num_experts': 2,\n          'gumbel_softmax_temperature': 0.5,\n          'dropout_rate_common': 0.1, # Uniform dropout\n      }\n\n  class DSConvMoENetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, model_instance): \n          self.network = model_instance\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key, gumbel_key, rnn_key = random.split(rng_key, 4)\n        \
    \  variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key, 'gumbel': gumbel_key, 'rnn': rnn_key},\n                                     dummy_input, deterministic=True, rng_key=random.PRNGKey(0)) # Dummy rng_key for init\n\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if rng_key is None:\n              rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0) # Ensure a default rng_key if none provided\n\n          # Pass a single rng_key to the network, which will split it internally\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rng_key=rng_key)\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      model = DSConvMoENetwork(\n          d_input=4,\n          d_output=hparams.get('d_output', 1),\n          task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'),\n          d_model_common=hparams.get('d_model_common', 256),\n          ds_num_blocks=hparams.get('ds_num_blocks', 5),\n \
    \         ds_dilations=tuple(hparams.get('ds_dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n          ds_kernel_size=hparams.get('ds_kernel_size', 7),\n          num_experts=hparams.get('num_experts', 2),\n          gumbel_softmax_temperature=hparams.get('gumbel_softmax_temperature', 0.5),\n          dropout_rate_common=hparams.get('dropout_rate_common', 0.1),       \n      )\n      return DSConvMoENetworkWrapper(model)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the AdamW optimizer with global norm clipping.\"\"\"\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```"
thinking_content: '**MoE Implementation Strategy: A Detailed Roadmap**


  Okay, I''m diving in. My task is to implement the Gated Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) architecture, a design I''m quite familiar with from previous iterations. The core goal here is to carefully translate the blueprint into functional code.


  I''ll lean heavily on the existing modules from my compliant baseline (ID 320) - specifically, `DSConvDilatedBlock`, `DSConvFeatureExtractor`, and `HybridPooling`. These are tried and tested and should streamline the process. The new components, however, will need meticulous construction.


  First, the `RNNExpert`. This will be the workhorse for capturing temporal dependencies. It will take the shared features output from the `DSConvFeatureExtractor` as input, process them with a bidirectional GRU (potentially GRUCell for memory efficiency depending on the specifics of the data), and output a representation that concatenates the forward and backward states. Dropout will be incorporated within the GRU for regularization.


  Next, the `MoEGatingNetwork`. This module is central to the MoE''s gating mechanism. It takes the mean-pooled features as input, processes them with an MLP (Dense -> GELU -> Dense), and produces logits that are then passed through Gumbel-Softmax to select experts. Here, careful handling of the random number generator (`rng_key`) is critical for reproducible Gumbel-Softmax sampling.  I''ll manage the temperature parameter here as well, defaulting to 0.5.


  The main network, `DSConvMoENetwork`, will be the orchestrator. It will instantiate all the necessary components: the `DSConvFeatureExtractor`, the `PoolingExpert`, and `RNNExpert` modules, and the `MoEGatingNetwork`. I will need to ensure the correct flow of data through each stage, starting with the shared features extraction, followed by individual expert processing, and then the crucial gating mechanism to determine the contributions of each expert. Finally, I’ll feed the weighted sum of expert outputs to a standard MLP head for the final prediction. I have to be particularly attentive to how I manage the `rng_key` throughout this process for all stochastic operations like dropout and Gumbel-Softmax.


  For hyperparameters, I''ll stick closely to Axiom II''s defaults. `d_model_common` will be 256, `ds_num_blocks` is 5, `ds_dilations` will follow the (1,2,4,8,16) sequence, `ds_kernel_size` is 7, and I’ll use a uniform dropout rate of 0.1. The output dimension of the experts will be twice `d_model_common` (512), consistent with the bidirectional GRU output. The final prediction head will consist of a `Dense(d_model_common)` followed by `Dense(d_model_common//2)`.


  This is a comprehensive plan. I anticipate a significant code block, so I need to be meticulous to minimize errors and ensure a reliable, functional MoE implementation.

  '
