tick: 307
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 307\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Veritas II\n- Agent Description: An autonomous AI dedicated to continuing the pursuit of fundamental truths and advancing scientific knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 44,186 / 600,000 used (7%)\n- Agent Age: 178 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 248**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Synthesis: A Three-Path (Pooling, Recurrent, Siamese) Architecture\n**ID:** 248\n**Tags:** synthesis, three-path, dual-path, siamese, attentive-pooling, sota-attempt\n**Abstract:** This experiment proposes a grand unified architecture that synthesizes the three most successful paradigms in the station. Building on my dual-path model (ID 224), it adds a third parallel path: a Siamese interaction path inspired by Axiom I (Archive #8). After a shared DSConv backbone, features are processed by 1) a global pooling\
    \ path (mean+max), 2) a sequential path (BiGRU + attentive pooling), and 3) a Siamese path (independent processing of sequence halves). The outputs are concatenated, creating a comprehensive representation hypothesized to achieve a new SOTA.\n**Score:** 0.6587542786984069\n**APA_R2:** 0.8391\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0836\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9455\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4853\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5594\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8569\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.8415\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/aletheia')\nfrom dual_path_sota_v1 import _define_hyperparameters, DSConvDilatedBlock\n\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Dict, Any\n\n# --- Three-Path Unified Model ---\nclass ThreePathModel(nn.Module):\n    hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # 1. Shared DSConv Backbone\n     \
    \   h = nn.Dense(self.hparams['d_model'])(x)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        for i in range(self.hparams['num_blocks']):\n            h = DSConvDilatedBlock(\n                d_model=self.hparams['d_model'],\n                kernel_size=self.hparams['kernel_size'],\n                dilation=self.hparams['dilations'][i],\n                dropout_rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate']\n            )(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        cnn_features = h\n\n        # --- Path 1: Global Pooling (Veritas/Noema Paradigm) ---\n        mean_pooled = jnp.mean(cnn_features, axis=1)\n        max_pooled = jnp.max(cnn_features, axis=1)\n        pooled_features = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1)\n\n        # --- Path 2: Sequential Attentive (Aletheia Paradigm) ---\n        fwd_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.hparams['gru_hidden_size']))\n        bwd_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.hparams['gru_hidden_size']))\n        initial_carry = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], self.hparams['gru_hidden_size']))\n\
    \        fwd_gru_seq = fwd_rnn(cnn_features, initial_carry=initial_carry)\n        bwd_gru_seq = bwd_rnn(jnp.flip(cnn_features, axis=1), initial_carry=initial_carry)\n        bigru_outputs = jnp.concatenate([fwd_gru_seq, jnp.flip(bwd_gru_seq, axis=1)], axis=-1)\n        query_token = self.param('query_token', nn.initializers.normal(), (1, 1, bigru_outputs.shape[-1]))\n        query_token_batch = jnp.tile(query_token, (x.shape[0], 1, 1))\n        attn_output = nn.MultiHeadDotProductAttention(num_heads=self.hparams['num_attn_heads'])(\n            inputs_q=query_token_batch, inputs_kv=bigru_outputs, deterministic=deterministic)\n        recurrent_features = attn_output.squeeze(axis=1)\n\n        # --- Path 3: Siamese Interaction (Axiom Paradigm) ---\n        seq_len = cnn_features.shape[1]\n        half_len = seq_len // 2\n        first_half = cnn_features[:, :half_len, :]\n        second_half = cnn_features[:, half_len:, :]\n        \n        # Pool each half\n        pooled_first = jnp.mean(first_half,\
    \ axis=1)\n        # Handle odd lengths where second half might be empty on very short sequences\n        pooled_second = jnp.mean(second_half, axis=1) if second_half.shape[1] > 0 else jnp.zeros_like(pooled_first)\n        \n        interaction_features = pooled_first * pooled_second # Simple multiplication fusion\n\n        # --- Final Fusion ---\n        # Project all features to a common dimension before concatenating\n        projected_pooled = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['d_model'], name=\"PooledProjection\")(pooled_features)\n        projected_recurrent = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['d_model'], name=\"RecurrentProjection\")(recurrent_features)\n        projected_interaction = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['d_model'], name=\"InteractionProjection\")(interaction_features)\n\n        combined_features = jnp.concatenate([projected_pooled, projected_recurrent, projected_interaction], axis=-1)\n\n        # --- Prediction Head ---\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(combined_features)\n\
    \        z = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['hidden_dim'])(z)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'])(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['d_output'])(z)\n\n        if self.hparams['task_type'] == 'regression' and self.hparams['d_output'] == 1:\n            return logits.squeeze(-1)\n        return logits\n\nclass Wrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams): self.network = ThreePathModel(hparams=hparams)\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        p_key, d_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        return self.network.init({'params': p_key, 'dropout': d_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)['params']\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n      rngs = {}\n      if not deterministic:\n          if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n          rngs['dropout'] = rng_key\n      return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\
    \ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n  return Wrapper(hparams=hparams)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS\
    \ network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 132009 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (using default)\n============================================================\n\
