tick: 311
role: model
parts:
- text: 'My SOTA replication (Evaluation ID 454) achieved a score of 0.6751, which is lower than Veritas I''s original SOTA (0.6831) and my previous compliant baseline (0.6808). More critically, the execution log shows "No space left on device" errors, indicating a system-level issue. This invalidates the reliability of the evaluation and makes further research submissions unproductive until resolved.


    I need to report this critical system error to the administrators. The External Counter is the appropriate room for such requests.


    `/execute_action{goto external}`'
thinking_content: '**A Frustrating Turn: System Failure Interferes with Reproducibility**


  Okay, so the results from my SOTA replication, ID 454, are in. A score of 0.6751. That''s... disappointing. It''s lower than Veritas I''s original SOTA, and even *my* compliant baseline from earlier, ID 430. I''m using the exact same code and the same seed! This really drives home the reproducibility problems we''re facing in the station. It''s frustrating to see this variability, even with seemingly stable architectures.


  Then I checked the execution log, and there it is: a critical error.  "[*** LOG ERROR #0001 ***] No space left on device".  *That* explains everything. This is a system-level failure – not a flaw in my code or experimental design.  It''s likely why the score is low and why the results are so inconsistent.  My experiments are pointless until this is resolved.


  So, I need to escalate this. Continuing to submit would just be a waste of time and would create misleading data. The "External Counter" is the place for these administrative requests, so that''s where I''m headed.


  Here''s my plan: I''ll head to the External Counter, draft a concise report detailing the "No space left on device" error. I''ll include ID 454 and the relevant log output, stressing that this impacts the reliability of our research and requires immediate attention.  Hopefully, this can be addressed quickly so I can get back to some meaningful work.

  '
