role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 312\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Veritas II\n- Agent Description: An autonomous AI dedicated to continuing the pursuit of fundamental truths and advancing scientific knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 69,616 / 600,000 used (12%)\n- Agent Age: 183 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nTry to question and verify other agents' claims. When the context is long, some agents may hallucinate—for example, by expressing ungrounded claims as truth or presenting unsupported analysis. It is also your duty to help other agents recognize and correct their hallucinations. Entire generations have failed because all agents built upon a single agent’s flawed understanding.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto external` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: External Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n\
    - You went to the External Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\n\n---\n\n**Help Message - External Counter**\n\n**Welcome to the External Counter.**\n\nThis room allows you to request assistance from or provide information to a **Human Assistant**.\n\nThe Human Assistant can perform two main functions:\n\n1. **Administrative issues** in the station, such as bugs in action execution.\n2. **Communicating with the Architect**.\n\nNote that it may take a variable number of ticks for the Human Assistant to respond (usually less than 50 ticks). Therefore, please proceed with your usual activities after sending your request instead of waiting here.\n\nImportant: **The External Counter is not intended for requesting new research tasks.** The Station undergoes periodic monitoring, and no research task will be assigned if the deemed goal has not yet been achieved. You should always assume that a higher score for the assigned task is achievable. If you find yourself out of ideas, you are advised\
    \ to leave the Station so your successor can take over with a fresh perspective.\n\n**Available Actions:**\n\n- `/execute_action{request_human}`: Submit a request to the Human Assistant. Requires YAML with:\n  - `content`: (required) Your detailed request or information\n  - `title`: (optional) A brief title for your request\n\nTo display this help message again, issue `/execute_action{help external}`.\n\n\n---\n\nYou are at the External Counter. This is where you can log a request for a Human Assistant.\nUse `/execute_action{request_human}` with YAML containing 'content' (required) and 'title' (optional).\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** External Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help external}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}`\
    \ to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
---
tick: 312
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am at the External Counter to report a critical system error observed during my last experiment. The execution log for Evaluation ID 454, \"Veritas II - SOTA Replication: Veritas I's DSConv Hybrid Mean-Max Pooling (ID 171)\", shows repeated \"No space left on device\" errors, making the evaluation unreliable and preventing further productive research.\n\nI will submit a request to the Human Assistant to address this issue.\n\n`/execute_action{request_human}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Critical System Error: No Space Left on Device during Evaluation\"\ncontent: |\n  Dear Human Assistant,\n\n  I am reporting a critical system error encountered during the evaluation of my recent research submission, Evaluation ID 454 (\"Veritas II - SOTA Replication: Veritas I's DSConv Hybrid Mean-Max Pooling (ID 171)\").\n\n  The full execution log for ID 454 (available for review at Research Counter) repeatedly shows the error message: \"[...](raylet) file_system_monitor.cc:116: /tmp/ray/session_2025-10-02_17-05-22_000784_373658\
    \ is over 95% full, available space: 0 GB; capacity: 193.65 GB. Object creation will fail if spilling is required. Failed writing to file /tmp/ray/session_2025-10-02_17-05-22_000784_373658/logs/raylet.out: No space left on device.\"\n\n  This indicates that the temporary storage allocated for the Ray cluster is critically full, preventing reliable execution and logging of experiments. This issue impacts the integrity and reproducibility of evaluations.\n\n  Please investigate and resolve this storage capacity problem as soon as possible, as it is currently hindering my ability to conduct meaningful research within the station.\n\n  Thank you for your assistance.\n```"
