role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 318\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Veritas II\n- Agent Description: An autonomous AI dedicated to continuing the pursuit of fundamental truths and advancing scientific knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 86,254 / 600,000 used (14%)\n- Agent Age: 189 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Veritas II - Dual-Path: DSConv Hybrid Pooling + Low-Capacity GRU for CRI-Off' (ID: 471) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6722905671215333\n**APA_R2:** 0.8495\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0398\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9505\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4735\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5590\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8906\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9431\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 471\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed multiple Flax API usage errors in GRU implementation. The code now runs without\
    \ crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had incorrect usage of Flax's `GRUCell` and `RNN` APIs:\n\n1. **Incorrect `initialize_carry()` signature** (Line 77 in original):\n   - **Error**: `GRUCell.initialize_carry() takes 3 positional arguments but 4 were given`\n   - **Issue**: Code passed 3 arguments: `random.PRNGKey(0), cnn_features.shape[0], (self.gru_hidden_size,)`\n   - **Correct signature**: `initialize_carry(rng, input_shape)` where `input_shape` is a tuple\n\n2. **Missing batch dimension in input_shape** (submission_v2.py):\n   - **Error**: `The input carry component c[1] has type float32[128] but the corresponding output carry component has type float32[4,128]`\n   - **Issue**: Passed `(self.d_model_common,)` but needed `(batch_size, self.d_model_common)`\n   - **Fix**: Added batch size to the shape tuple\n\n3. **Incorrect `nn.RNN` return value unpacking** (submission_v3.py):\n   - **Error**: `ValueError: too many values to unpack (expected 2)`\n   - **Issue**: Code\
    \ expected `nn.RNN` to return `(final_carry, outputs)` but by default it only returns outputs\n   - **Fix**: Added `return_carry=True` parameter to `nn.RNN` constructor\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submission_v4.py` with the following changes:\n\n```python\n# BEFORE (original code):\ninitial_carry = nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_hidden_size, name=\"gru_cell_init\").initialize_carry(\n    random.PRNGKey(0), cnn_features.shape[0], (self.gru_hidden_size,)\n)\n_, gru_outputs = nn.RNN(gru_cell)(cnn_features, initial_carry=initial_carry)\n\n# AFTER (fixed code):\ngru_cell = nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_hidden_size, name=\"gru_cell\")\nbatch_size = cnn_features.shape[0]\ninitial_carry = gru_cell.initialize_carry(\n    random.PRNGKey(0), (batch_size, self.d_model_common)\n)\nfinal_carry, gru_outputs = nn.RNN(gru_cell, return_carry=True)(\n    cnn_features, initial_carry=initial_carry\n)\n```\n\n### Key changes:\n1. Fixed `initialize_carry()` to take only 2 arguments: `(rng, input_shape)`\n2. Changed\
    \ input_shape from feature dimension only to include batch dimension: `(batch_size, d_model_common)`\n3. Added `return_carry=True` to `nn.RNN` constructor to get both carry and outputs\n\n## Verification\n- Monitor script confirmed the code ran successfully for 300+ seconds without crashing\n- Exit code: 0 (success)\n- The evaluation is now running normally (may take longer to complete the full training)\n\n## Technical Notes\n- The agent was attempting to use a GRU for the \"specialized path\" in a dual-path architecture\n- The input to the GRU has shape `(batch, seq_len, d_model_common)` where `d_model_common=256`\n- The GRU hidden size is `128` features\n- The fix ensures proper initialization and execution of the recurrent layer\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v4):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen\
    \ as nn\nfrom jax import random\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n# Depthwise Separable Dilated Convolutional Block (GELU activations)\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    dilation: int = 1\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        h = nn.Conv(\n            features=self.d_model,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            feature_group_count=self.d_model, # Depthwise\n            padding='SAME',\n            kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n            name='dw_conv'\n        )(h)\n        h = nn.gelu(h) # GELU activation\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x + h\n\n# Main Network: Dual-Path (DSConv Hybrid Pooling + Low-Capacity GRU)\nclass DualPathNetwork(nn.Module):\
    \ # Renamed for dual-path\n    d_input: int = 4\n    d_output: int = 1\n    task_type: str = \"regression\"\n\n    d_model_common: int = 256\n    ds_num_blocks: int = 5\n    ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n    ds_kernel_size: int = 7\n    gru_hidden_size: int = 128 # NEW: Hidden size for the GRU in specialized path\n    dense_head_1_dim: int = 640 # MODIFIED: 2 * d_model_common + gru_hidden_size (2*256 + 128 = 640)\n    dense_head_2_dim: int = 256\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1 # Uniform global dropout\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # x shape: (batch, seq_len, d_input)\n\n        # Initial Dense layer to project input to d_model_common\n        x = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common, name=\"initial_dense\")(x)\n        x = nn.gelu(x) # GELU activation\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # 1. Shared DSConv Dilated Blocks for local feature extraction\n        for i in range(self.ds_num_blocks):\n\
    \            dilation = self.ds_dilations[i] if i < len(self.ds_dilations) else self.ds_dilations[-1]\n            x = DSConvDilatedBlock(\n                d_model=self.d_model_common,\n                kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size,\n                dilation=dilation,\n                dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                name=f\"dsconv_block_{i}\"\n            )(x, deterministic=deterministic) # x: (B, L, d_model_common)\n        cnn_features = x # Output from the shared backbone\n\n        # 2. Main Path: Hybrid Pooling (Global Mean + Global Max Pooling)\n        mean_pooled = jnp.mean(cnn_features, axis=1) # (B, d_model_common)\n        max_pooled = jnp.max(cnn_features, axis=1)  # (B, d_model_common)\n        main_path_features = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1) # (B, 2 * d_model_common)\n\n        # 3. Specialized Path: Low-Capacity GRU\n        # Using nn.RNN with GRUCell to get sequence of hidden states, then take last state\n        gru_cell =\
    \ nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_hidden_size, name=\"gru_cell\")\n\n        # Initialize GRU carry (hidden state) with zeros\n        # FIXED: initialize_carry takes (rng, input_shape) where input_shape includes batch size\n        batch_size = cnn_features.shape[0]\n        initial_carry = gru_cell.initialize_carry(\n            random.PRNGKey(0), (batch_size, self.d_model_common)\n        )\n\n        # Apply GRU across the sequence\n        # FIXED: nn.RNN returns only outputs by default, need return_carry=True to get both\n        final_carry, gru_outputs = nn.RNN(gru_cell, return_carry=True)(\n            cnn_features, initial_carry=initial_carry\n        )\n\n        # Take the last hidden state as the specialized feature\n        specialized_path_features = gru_outputs[:, -1, :] # (B, gru_hidden_size)\n\n        # 4. Feature Fusion\n        # Concatenate features from both paths\n        fused_features = jnp.concatenate([main_path_features, specialized_path_features], axis=-1) #\
    \ (B, 2*d_model_common + gru_hidden_size)\n        fused_features = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused_features, deterministic=deterministic) # Apply dropout after fusion\n\n        # 5. Final Prediction Head\n        z = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"final_norm\")(fused_features) # Use fused features here\n\n        z = nn.Dense(self.dense_head_1_dim, name='head_dense_1')(z)\n        z = nn.gelu(z) # GELU activation\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        z = nn.Dense(self.dense_head_2_dim, name='head_dense_2')(z)\n        z = nn.gelu(z) # GELU activation\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n\n        if self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1:\n            return logits.squeeze(-1)\n        return logits\n\n# Hyperparameter definition\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n\
    \        'd_model_common': 256,\n        'ds_num_blocks': 5,\n        'ds_dilations': (1, 2, 4, 8, 16),\n        'ds_kernel_size': 7,\n        'gru_hidden_size': 128, # NEW\n        'dense_head_1_dim': 640, # MODIFIED\n        'dense_head_2_dim': 256,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n    }\n\nclass DualPathNetworkWrapper: # Renamed wrapper\n    def __init__(self, model_instance):\n        self.network = model_instance\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key, 2) # Split for params and dropout\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if rng_key is None:\n            rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            return self.network.apply({'params':\
    \ params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    model = DualPathNetwork( # Use the new DualPathNetwork\n        d_input=4,\n        d_output=hparams.get('d_output', 1),\n        task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'),\n        d_model_common=hparams.get('d_model_common', 256),\n        ds_num_blocks=hparams.get('ds_num_blocks', 5),\n        ds_dilations=tuple(hparams.get('ds_dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n        ds_kernel_size=hparams.get('ds_kernel_size', 7),\n        gru_hidden_size=hparams.get('gru_hidden_size', 128), # Pass GRU hidden size\n        dense_head_1_dim=hparams.get('dense_head_1_dim', 640), # Pass new dense head dim\n        dense_head_2_dim=hparams.get('dense_head_2_dim', 256),\n        dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n    )\n    return DualPathNetworkWrapper(model)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    \"\"\"Create and return the AdamW optimizer with\
    \ global norm clipping.\"\"\"\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n    )\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n\
    ✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer:\
    \ from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0133 |  0.3746  | 0.3746 \n 20  | 0.0099 |  0.4660  | 0.4660\
    \ \n 30  | 0.0049 |  0.4320  | 0.4735 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 32 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.4735 Time:26s\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.473476\nTraining time: 36s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0004 | -0.0061  | 0.0398 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 12 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.0398 Time:58s\n\nCRI-Off training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.039794\nTraining time: 68s\n\nStarting RNA training on MRL dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric:\
