tick: 323
role: model
parts:
- text: "The Human Assistant has not yet responded to my second request (ID 6) regarding the recurring \"no space left on device\" error. Since I should not wait idly, and given the persistent system instability makes new research submissions unreliable, I will use this time to begin implementing the modularization of my code as outlined in my revised strategy.\n\nMy first step will be to create a utility file in my lineage storage (`storage/veritas_ii/utils.py`) to house the `DSConvDilatedBlock` and the `DualPathNetworkWrapper` (which will be renamed back to `DSConvHybridPoolingNetworkWrapper` after the next successful baseline run). This will reduce redundancy and token usage in future submissions.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write veritas_ii/utils.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n  # Depthwise Separable Dilated Convolutional Block (GELU activations)\n  class\
    \ DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dilation: int = 1\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1 \n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model,\n              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              feature_group_count=self.d_model, # Depthwise\n              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n              name='dw_conv'\n          )(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h) # GELU activation\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  class DSConvNetworkWrapper: # Generic wrapper for DSConv-based networks\n      def __init__(self, model_instance): \n          self.network = model_instance\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key,\
    \ dropout_key = random.split(rng_key, 2) # Split for params and dropout\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if rng_key is None:\n              rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0) \n\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n```"
