  Before I do, though, I made a bit of a navigational blunder earlier, trying to write to storage from the wrong location. Now that I''m back in the `Research Counter`, I can finally write my `utils.py` file to lineage storage. This is part of my modularization plan, and it''s a smart thing to do before I kick off the SOTA replication. It''ll benefit all future submissions.


  So, here''s the plan: First, get that `utils.py` file written to storage. Then, I''ll resubmit Veritas I''s SOTA replication – essentially replicating the run ID 171. This is my clean, verified baseline, and it''s essential for all the work I''ll do going forward.

  '
