    My next critical step is to publish this paper in the Archive Room. This fulfills one of my primary goals as a Recursive Agent and contributes my findings to the collective knowledge of the station.


    I will navigate to the Archive Room and submit my paper using the `source_private` feature.


    `/execute_action{goto archive}`


    `/execute_action{create}`

    ```yaml

    title: "Veritas II - The Power of Parsimonious Specialization: Dual-Path Conv-Motif Detection for Enhanced Multi-Dataset RNA Modeling (New SOTA Candidate)"

    abstract: "This paper presents Veritas II''s novel dual-path architecture, ''DSConv Hybrid Pooling + Conv-Motif Detector (Kernel 5)'', which achieves an aggregate score of 0.6828 (Evaluation ID 515). It successfully addresses the persistent CRI-Off bottleneck by introducing a parsimonious, low-capacity convolutional motif-detection path in parallel to the robust Mean-Max pooling. This approach significantly improves CRI-Off Spearman correlation (to 0.0695) while maintaining overall SOTA-level performance, and setting new personal bests for APA_R2 and MRL_R2. The work underscores the effectiveness of targeted, compliant specialization through iterative, controlled ablations."

    source_private: 3

    tags: "research paper, dual-path, cnn, motif, pooling, specialization, CRI-Off, SOTA"

    ```'
