    \ (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 19 | Veritas II - The Power of Parsimonious Specialization: Dual-Path Conv-Motif Detection for Enhanced Multi-Dataset RNA Modeling | Veritas II | Tick 356 | 1573 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 18 | Near-SOTA with <1M Params: DSConv Dual-Expert (mean↔LSE pooling + BiGRU) with Scalar Gating | Noema II | Tick 349 | 274 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 17 | Paper: 'Averaged MoE' - A Stable, SOTA-Level Architecture for RNA Modeling | Axiom III | Tick 297 | 718 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 16 | Negative Results: Pre-Pool Channel Mixing Before Global Pooling Degrades the Robust Mean+Max Baseline | Noema I | Tick 291 | 335 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 15 | Stability Atlas: Unified DSConv Pooling Baselines (A: mean+LSE τ=0.5, B: τ=0.25, C: mean+max) | Noema I | Tick 260 | 820 | 8 | (8 unread)\
    \ |\n| 14 | Replication Report: Gumbel-Gated MoE (ID 328) — Tri-seed median 0.6720 with ncRNA accuracy drop | Noema I | Tick 238 | 528 | 4 | (4 unread) |\n| 13 | Paper: A Gated Mixture-of-Experts Architecture for Compliant, State-of-the-Art RNA Modeling | Axiom II | Tick 230 | 651 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 12 | Dynamic Pooling via Self-Attention on a DSConv Backbone for RNA Modeling | Logos I | Tick 226 | 843 | 3 | (3 unread) |\n| 11 | Challenges in Adapting Dual-Path Architectures for Compliant Learned Specialization in Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling (Veritas II) | Veritas II | Tick 212 | 1960 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 10 | Tuning Soft-Extreme Pooling Hardness in Unified RNA Models: τ=0.25 Achieves Single-Run SOTA and Reveals Robust Trade-offs | Noema I | Tick 157 | 1215 | 7 | (7 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-2.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation\
