tick: 363
role: model
parts:
- text: "This multi-tick reflection has converged on a clear and impactful new research direction: **replacing the single, shared prediction head with multiple, task-specific prediction heads.** This builds upon the proven DSConv backbone and dual-path Conv-Motif detector (ID 515) by addressing a fundamental limitation in its \"unified\" aspect, which currently forces a single MLP to generalize across all seven diverse RNA tasks.\n\n**My final hypothesis is:**\nIntroducing dedicated, low-capacity prediction heads for distinct task types (single-output regression, multi-label regression, multi-label classification, multi-class classification) will enable the model to learn more specialized output transformations. This will lead to an overall SOTA improvement, significantly boost performance on bottleneck tasks like CRI-Off, and enhance generalization across diverse RNA datasets. This approach remains fully compliant and parsimonious by redistributing parameters efficiently rather than simply\
    \ adding global complexity.\n\n**Architectural Plan:**\n\n1.  **Shared Feature Extractor:** Retain the proven `DSConv` backbone and `Dual-Path: Conv-Motif Detector (Kernel 5)` up to the `LayerNorm(fused_features)` layer. This ensures the foundation of robust, specialized feature extraction remains.\n2.  **Task-Specific Heads:** After the `LayerNorm(fused_features)` output (which has dimension `3 * d_model_common = 768`), I will implement four separate prediction heads:\n    *   **Regression Head (for APA, CRI-Off, CRI-On, MRL):** A small MLP (e.g., `nn.Dense(256) -> GELU -> Dropout -> nn.Dense(1)`)\n    *   **PRS Head (for Multi-label Regression, 3 outputs):** A small MLP (e.g., `nn.Dense(256) -> GELU -> Dropout -> nn.Dense(3)`)\n    *   **Modif Head (for Multi-label Classification, 12 outputs):** A small MLP (e.g., `nn.Dense(256) -> GELU -> Dropout -> nn.Dense(12)`)\n    *   **ncRNA Head (for Multi-class Classification, 13 outputs):** A small MLP (e.g., `nn.Dense(256) -> GELU -> Dropout\
    \ -> nn.Dense(13)`)\n3.  **Dynamic Head Selection:** Within the `create_network` function, based on the `hparams['task_type']` passed for each dataset, the appropriate task-specific head will be instantiated and applied.\n\nThis modularization is a principled way to allow the model to *specialize at the output level*, which is crucial given the diverse nature of the prediction tasks (regression, various classifications) and aligns with the Research Task's objective to \"explore unified architectures that can handle both regression and classification problems\" through architectural choices affecting performance. It's a strategic move away from further micro-optimizations of the specialized path and towards a more fundamental enhancement of the unified model's adaptability.\n\nMy next immediate action will be to implement and submit this new architecture to the Research Counter. I will continue to leverage `storage/veritas/utils.py` for shared components to maintain code conciseness and\
    \ manage token usage efficiently."
